{{!-- The Post Surface's body, in the Layout it is handed.

`layout` is `@custom.post_layout` from post.hbs, or a fixed value from a Layout override template
(ADR 0006); the {{#match}} is the pattern home.hbs documents. `{{#post}}` changes the context, so
the argument is read one frame up, as `../layout`.

What is on this page below the article — the writer, the neighbours, three more posts, the
subscribe band — is the same in both layouts and belongs to neither, so it is called here once.
Only the reading column differs, which is the whole of what A1 and A2 are. --}}
	{{#post}}
		<article class="{{post_class}}" data-surface="post">
			{{#match ../layout "Title page"}}
				{{> "post/a2"}}
			{{else}}
				{{> "post/a1"}}
			{{/match}}
		</article>

		{{> "post/related"}}

		{{> "newsletter" anchor="end-newsletter"}}
	{{/post}}
